==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|parasitisme|lang=fr}}. Surface etymology is {{suffix|parasite|ism|lang=en}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{context|ecology|lang=en}} Interaction between two organisms, in which one organism (the [[parasite]]) benefits and the other (the [[host]]) is harmed.
# {{context|figuratively|lang=en}} A similar interaction between people.
#: ''We accused her of '''parasitism''' in taking his hard-earned money for new dresses.''

